cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the associated manuscript and this software archive."
title: "qm-odor-prediction: quantum-mechanical descriptor-enhanced molecular representations for odor prediction"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/BlOON-1/qm-odor-prediction"
version: "0.1.0"
license: "CC-BY-NC-4.0"
abstract: "This repository provides code, environment specifications, and processed-data documentation for reproducing benchmark odor prediction, structure-neighborhood discrimination, external sensory-panel validation, and orthogonal consistency analysis against public receptor-response annotations using quantum-mechanical descriptor-enhanced molecular representations. The manuscript-aligned release contains 4,495 curated benchmark molecules, 112 standardized odor labels used for modeling, 87 structurally similar external molecules arranged into 60 comparison pairs, and a 43-label sensory vocabulary."
keywords:
  - odor prediction
  - quantum-mechanical descriptors
  - molecular representation
  - multi-label classification
  - olfactory receptors
  - structural neighborhoods
  - RDKit
  - graph neural networks
